  "methodology": "Windows Process.PrivateMemorySize64 and WorkingSet64 for process IDs reported by each isolated Chromium process. Two-second delay after each bounded sample; no per-sample history retained. Bracketed phase transitions, explicit missing-ID/error tracking. Main-page GC only after timed work, with before/after process and CDP snapshots.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single trials, one host, bundled HeadlessChrome 153.0.8010.12, synthetic sources and direct harness SDP exchange.",
    "100 MiB and 1 GiB include OPFS destination save and independent byte audit; 5 GiB is receive/whole-stream verification only.",
    "Periodic sampling can miss peaks and processes created between observations. Working-set sums can double-count shared resident pages and are not unique machine RAM.",
    "Observer CPU/IPC overhead affects timings; these are diagnostic rates, not matched optimization or LAN speed acceptance.",
    "Forced collection is diagnostic and is not part of production transfer. Worker/native allocations are not all forced to collect.",
    "The historical 728 MB 5 GiB full-save/audit heap peak remains retained; this run neither repeats that entire scope nor proves it fixed.",
    "50–100 GB+, native Windows folders, physical networks/devices, hosted CI, updated isolated install, usability and broader adversarial acceptance remain unproven."
  ],
